NiceMon V9.9
HELP lists the statements
READY.
help
SYS A               call the program at A, such as SYS 0x8000; SYS 0 restarts
LOAD                enter lines of ADDR WORD in hex, as a .bin file has them
LOAD "NAME.BIN"     load the .bin file NAME.BIN of the SD card
LOAD "N.BIN", "IP"  load the .bin file N.BIN from the TFTP server at IP
SAVE "NAME", A, N   save N words from A as the .bin file NAME
DELETE "NAME"       delete the file NAME of the SD card
DIR [SLOT]          list the files of the card in SLOT, or of the card mounted
DIR "IP" [, "PAT"]  list the files of tools/tftpd.py at IP, or those of PAT
DUMP [A] [, N]      show N words from A, in hex, or the next ones
DIS [A] [, N]       disassemble N instructions from A, or the next ones
IP ["A.B.C.D"]      show the IP address, or set it, such as "192.168.1.65"
DHCP                get the IP address from a DHCP server
MAC ["MAC"]         show the MAC address, or set it, "02:4E:49:43:45:01"
BAUD [RATE]         show the UART baud rate, or set it, such as 921600
TIME ["D T"]        show the local time, or set it, "2026-11-11 14:30:00"
NTP ["S"] [, "Z"]   set it from time server S, Z local time less UTC, "+01:00"
CLS                 clear the screen
VER                 the version
HALT                halt the core
HELP                the statements
CRSR up down        scroll back a row, before a statement
PgUp PgDn           a page; on the MEGA65 CTRL and MEGA with CRSR up or down
